Consider adding a `validate` callback to the features input prompt to ensure at least one feature is provided, mirroring the validation applied for other required fields.
```suggestion
      message: 'Main features (comma-separated):',
      validate: (input) => {
        const features = input
          .split(',')
          .map((f: string) => f.trim())
          .filter((f: string) => f);
        return features.length > 0 ? undefined : 'At least one feature is required';
      },
```
